A world jog under the tool centre point slows to a stop where a joint
reaches its soft limit, as a jog of a slide does at its axis limit, and a
jog away from the limit is free.

The jog test's machine (5axiskins, 400 mm pivot, the head laid over to
B90 by a joint move, the joints following through limit3) with joint 1
given 300 mm of travel each way, so a jog of C with the tip held swings
the carriage out of it about 48.6 degrees round.  In teleop mode: a
continuous jog of C held well past that, an incremental jog of 20 degrees
away, an incremental jog of 60 back towards the limit, and one away again.
The test asserts that each jog into the limit comes to rest with joint 1
within 1 micron inside its limit and never past it, that the jog has
ended there and says nothing (no soft limit error, no following error),
that the jogs away land where they were sent, and that no joint's
commanded velocity or acceleration went over its INI limit.
